+# Manually dispatched, staging-only rehearsal of the backup path:
+#
+#   disposable PostgreSQL 17  <-  decrypt + restore + verify
+#        ^                                   |
+#        |                          download newest object
+#   Backblaze B2 (bucket, region: environment-designated)
+#        ^
+#   encrypted backup taken from the designated STAGING Supabase project
+#
+# Registration and dispatch
+# ------------------------
+# GitHub registers manual workflows from the DEFAULT BRANCH. Until this file
+# is merged to `main`, it is dispatchable only when a registration patch that
+# adds this exact file is applied to `main`. Dispatching requires explicit
+# owner authorization; dispatching reads STAGING data, creates a real B2
+# object and may incur charges. No remote pruning is ever performed here.
+#
+# Exact-code / ref validation
+# ---------------------------
+# The `ref` input accepts a full 40-character lowercase hex commit SHA only
+# (branch names, tags and short SHAs are refused). When empty, it resolves to
+# the commit this workflow runs at (for the default-branch registration, the
+# default-branch tip). The `exact-code-gate` job then fetches EXACTLY that
+# commit and refuses to proceed unless the fetched tree carries, byte for
+# byte, the audited V3 staging implementation pinned below (every file
+# first-party code would execute, plus package.json / package-lock.json).
+# After the gate passes, the rehearsal job checks out that exact SHA and runs
+# whatever it contains. If the ref does not contain the V3 implementation —
+# for example today's `main`, which lacks `validate-staging-source.mjs` and
+# has older backup scripts — the gate fails closed BEFORE any credential is
+# materialized anywhere. The gate job holds no environment, secret or
+# variable.
+#
+# When the pinned implementation changes, the manifest below (and the
+# `staging-rehearsal-wiring.test.mjs` guard that re-derives it from the tree)
+# must be regenerated in the SAME change. Never edit the manifest by hand.
+#
+# Environment gate and secrets
+# ----------------------------
+# The rehearsal job binds the protected `backup-staging` GitHub Environment
+# and consumes ONLY these environment secrets:
+#
+#   STAGING_AUTODINE_BACKUP_SOURCE_URL   designated staging read connection
+#   STAGING_AUTODINE_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE   backup encryption passphrase
+#   STAGING_B2_REGION                    staging bucket region
+#   STAGING_B2_BUCKET                    staging bucket (never a production one)
+#   STAGING_B2_ACCESS_KEY_ID             staging B2 application keyID
+#   STAGING_B2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY         staging B2 application key
+#
+# and ONLY these environment variables:
+#
+#   AUTODINE_STAGING_PROJECT_REF         20-char ref of the designated staging project
+#   AUTODINE_STAGING_B2_BUCKET           the same staging bucket name, designated again
+#   AUTODINE_PRODUCTION_B2_BUCKETS       JSON array of production bucket names (refusal list)
+#
+# No production secret name is referenced, `secrets: inherit` is never used,
+# and no value is printed, artifacted or passed to a step that does not need
+# it. The preflight step checks PRESENCE with GitHub boolean expressions —
+# the secret or variable VALUES never enter that step at all; it reports the
+# NAMES of anything missing and fails closed. The semantic check
+# (validate-staging-source.mjs) then proves the source URL targets the
+# designated staging project and the staging bucket, is not loopback, and is
+# not a production bucket — failing closed otherwise.
+#
+# Fallback posture (verified, with limits): GitHub falls back to a
+# repository-scoped secret/variable of the SAME NAME when the environment
+# does not define one. The names are uniquely STAGING_-prefixed and the
+# owner must not create repository copies; presence checks cannot distinguish
+# the two scopes, so the semantic validator and the production-bucket
+# refusal list are the second, independent layer. The workflow does NOT fall
+# back to: any unprefixed/production secret name, `.env` files (no backup
+# script loads one — guarded by test), a B2 endpoint override (not wired;
+# only official backblazeb2.com endpoints are accepted by the client), a
+# scratch/expected-ref opt-in, or any other environment (exactly one
+# `environment:` declaration exists, `backup-staging`).
+#
+# A 40-character `ref` that does not contain the V3 implementation is the
+# ONLY thing this workflow rehearses; see the gate. DO NOT dispatch without
+# explicit owner authorization. The PostgreSQL service is a disposable
+# loopback container; the restore target is loopback-only by guard and the
+# restore scripts refuse anything else.
